SUMMARY:Not One Less w/Q&A | For All the Children
DESCRIPTION:Wei Minzhi\, a 13‑year‑old substitute teacher\, must cove
 r a village school for one month and will not receive her salary if any o
 f the students drop out. When a boy leaves to seek work in a nearby city\
 , Wei follows to bring him back. Shot in a neorealist\, documentary style
 \, the film uses non-professional actors playing versions of themselves\,
  blurring the line between fiction and lived reality through simplicity\,
  restraint\, and careful observation of community. [106 min\; drama\; Man
 darin with English subtitles]A Q&amp\;A will follow the screening.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Wei Minzhi\, a 13‑year‑old substitu
 te teacher\, must cover a village school for one month and will not recei
 ve her salary if any of the students drop out. When a boy leaves to seek 
 work in a nearby city\, Wei follows to bring him back. Shot in a neoreali
 st\, documentary style\, the film uses non-professional actors playing ve
 rsions of themselves\, blurring the line between fiction and lived realit
 y through simplicity\, restraint\, and careful observation of community. 
 [106 min\; drama\; Mandarin with English subtitles]</p><p><i><strong>A Q&
 amp\;A will follow the screening.</strong></i></p>
