SUMMARY:Buck (2011) w/Q&A | Making Strides: Horses\, Healing\, and Commun
 ity
DESCRIPTION:American cowboy Buck Brannaman has a unique way of communicat
 ing with horses\, and it's exactly this unorthodox style of training that
  inspired the novel The Horse Whisperer. In this documentary\, director C
 indy Meehl gets to know the real-life Buck as she reveals his fascinating
  story about how an abusive childhood helped teach him the compassion and
  insight needed to train horses\, not with punishment but by treating the
 m the way he would treat humans—with respect. [88 min\; documentary\; E
 nglish]A Q&amp\;A with Lucy Downs (Sexual Assault Crisis Counselor\, IU C
 ounseling and Psychological Services) will follow the screening.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  American cowboy Buck Brannaman has a un
 ique way of communicating with horses\, and it's exactly this unorthodox 
 style of training that inspired the novel <i>The Horse Whisperer</i>. In 
 this documentary\, director Cindy Meehl gets to know the real-life Buck a
 s she reveals his fascinating story about how an abusive childhood helped
  teach him the compassion and insight needed to train horses\, not with p
 unishment but by treating them the way he would treat humans—with respe
 ct. [88 min\; documentary\; English]</p><p><i><strong>A Q&amp\;A with Luc
 y Downs (Sexual Assault Crisis Counselor\, IU Counseling and Psychologica
 l Services) will follow the screening.</strong></i></p>
