SUMMARY:Mulholland Drive w/Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:A complex tale of suspense set in sunshine-drenched Los Angel
 es\, the film follows a dark-haired amnesiac car crash victim and a blond
 e stranger who become new friends and investigatory partners as they atte
 mpt to solve the mystery of the dark-haired woman's true identity. In tru
 e Lynchian fashion\, this journey is an uneasy blend of innocence and cor
 ruption\, love and loneliness\, beauty and depravity. [147 min\; drama\; 
 English]The Cinema is pleased to welcome noted David Lynch scholar Dr. Ju
 stus Nieland\, who will introduce the film and take part in a post-film c
 onversation with Dr. Ed Dallis-Comentale\, Assistant Vice President for A
 rts and Humanities and Professor of English.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  A complex tale of suspense set in sunsh
 ine-drenched Los Angeles\, the film follows a dark-haired amnesiac car cr
 ash victim and a blonde stranger who become new friends and investigatory
  partners as they attempt to solve the mystery of the dark-haired woman's
  true identity. In true Lynchian fashion\, this journey is an uneasy blen
 d of innocence and corruption\, love and loneliness\, beauty and depravit
 y. [147 min\; drama\; English]</p><p><i><strong>The Cinema is pleased to 
 welcome noted David Lynch scholar Dr. Justus Nieland\, who will introduce
  the film and take part in a post-film conversation with Dr. Ed Dallis-Co
 mentale\, Assistant Vice President for Arts and Humanities and Professor 
 of English.</strong></i></p>
